     If you want slash'em, you know where to find it.

     I played it for a while several years ago, to see
whether there were features that nethack might "borrow".
Techniques weren't even close to making the cut.  Most of
them required spoilers to even figure out what they did,
and since I was playing unspoiled (except for assorted
bits pickup up from this newsgroup) I wasn't able to use
many of them.  Of the few I remember now, doppelganger's
liquid leap is the only one I actually made much use of,
and it was overpowered.  Jumping over monsters was very
valuable; there's really no need to splash acid on them
in the process.  And I don't want to think about how or
where I was spilling the acid from as I passed over....
Maybe you pass through rather than over, but that still
doesn't explain the acid.

     Vampire as a player race also has zero chance of
making it into nethack.  Offhand, amulet of flying was
the only thing I can recall wanting to add to nethack.
Corpses sometimes turning into mold monsters when rotting
away might be useful since that provides more vegetarian
fodder, but I think it would need to be changed to avoid
monster movement through corridors becoming blocked by
immobile critters.

     Unfortunately, whatever notes I made at the time
are on the hard drive of a PC which no longer boots, so
are effectively lost.  There's plenty of good stuff in
slash'em; unfortunately there's also lots of awful stuff.
I classify vampire for player race, potions of blood, and
medical kits as the latter.


